## A view on where the market is heading

"A price per metre is not enough on its own, for a buyer or for a developer. The difference between Piešťany and Banská Bystrica is exactly that: cheaper by the metre, dearer by the flat, because what gets built there is bigger. Compare towns by price per metre and you are comparing different goods," says Tomáš Kamhal, founder of Residata.

"The second thing the data shows every day is that developers do not cut prices. Of {moves90} price-list changes over three months, {movesUpPctEn}% were increases and the median change was {moveMedianPctEn}%. When a flat does not sell it stays on offer longer and the price list does not move down. So how long the supply takes to sell says more about this market than how many percent a price moved."

